				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody"><span style="font-weight: bold">Introduction</span>
<br />
Welcome to the new Clan MacLear Messageboards! EZ Board has served us well these many years, but we've gotten to the point where it's more cost effective to have our own boards, both in terms of cost, and wear and tear on the Administratrix.
<br />

<br />
This is a <a href="http://www.phpbb.com" target="_blank" class="postlink">phpBB messageboard</a> system, which is a free software package that's extremely customizable. There are thousands of modifications written by the developers and the user community that can add significant capabilities to our boards. As we go along, we'll be evaluating what new features might be useful and adding them. If you have any suggestions, please make a post or send me a private message and we'll talk it over.
<br />

<br />
There are tons of improvements over the EZBoard system, but most of them are behind the scenes, so the average user won't see them. There are a few things you need to know, however, so read on.
<br />

<br />
<span style="font-weight: bold">Usergroups</span>
<br />
It is every member's responsibility to join the Kin usergroup for any chapters that you wish to belong to. Membership in a Kin usergroup gives you access to that chapter's members-only forums. Nobles, Officers and Chiefs must also join the Kin usergroup(s) - they will then be assigned to the usergroup that matches their rank as well. 
<br />

<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Note: If you are not yet a full member of the Clan, then please do not apply for Usergroup access. Full membership means being ranked Kin in any of our chapters. If you're not sure whether you are Kin or not, then you probably are not, but please post in the public forum and we'll sort it out.</span>
<br />

<br />
To join, click on the "Usergroups" button at the top of the page. Select the Kin usergroup that you're interested in from the pull down menu and then click the "view information" button. Lastly, click on the "join group" button. Your membership must be approved by the moderator of that group, who is identified in the group information section. When you request to join a usergroup, an e-mail is sent to that moderator.
<br />

<br />
The available Kin usergroups are:
<br />

<br />
Kin - EQ
<br />
Kin - EQ2
<br />
Kin - DAoC
<br />
Kin - WoW
<br />

<br />
As Kin you have the right to join any or all of these groups if you wish. If you aren't playing a certain game, then I reccommend you do not join that group, simply to cut down on the number of forums that will show up on your index page.
<br />

<br />
<span style="font-weight: bold">Avatars</span>
<br />
An Avatar is a small picture that will show up beneath your rank in the poster information bar on the left. I've allowd everyone to upload an avatar that will be stored locally. The avatar file must be a .gif, .jpeg, or .png file. It must be 80 x 80 pixels maximum size, and it must be under 6KB maximum file size. These are pretty easy to achieve and you shouldn't have any problems with those limitations.
<br />

<br />
To upload an Avatar, click on the "Profile" button on the navigation bar at the top of the page. All the way at the bottom of the profile page is the Avatar control panel. you can upload something from your local machine or you can tell the system to download it from some URL that you supply.
<br />

<br />
You can change Avatars whenever you want, but you can only have one uploaded at a time.
<br />

<br />
<span style="font-weight: bold">Photo Gallery</span>
<br />
This messageboard is equiped with Photo Album software. To view the albums, click on the "Gallery" button at the top of the page. There are 5 categories - Everquest, Everquest2, Dark Age of Camelot, World of Warcraft, and Miscellaneous. Currently any Kin or above is allowed to upload photos within the following limitations:
<br />

<br />
Pictures must be .png, .jpg, or .gif files.
<br />
Pictures must be no larger than 800 x 600 pixels.
<br />
Pictures must be no larger than 128 KB.
<br />
Each Kin is limited to 50 pictures at any given time.
<br />

<br />
These are basically the defaults for the software, and we can adjust the limitations as we find need to do so.
<br />

<br />
To upload photos, simply click on the album you want to upload to, click the "upload pictures" button and follow the prompts.<div style="vertical-align: bottom"><br /><br /><br />_________________<br />- Jalia</div></span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
